@startuml 06_fetch_add_vs_cas
title 6. Two ways to make x = x + 1 atomic
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF

start
if (which way?) then (fetch_add)
  :one instruction: lock add $1, (x)\nhardware does load, add, store as one step;
  stop
else (CAS loop)
  :expected = load x;
  repeat
    :new = expected + 1;
    :compare_exchange(x, expected, new)\nlock cmpxchg;
  repeat while (swap failed?) is (yes: retry with the value that won)
  :done;
  stop
endif

footer fetch_add is 1 instruction (about 1.3 ns uncontended). CAS does a load plus lock cmpxchg and may retry. With two threads CAS was about 2.6x slower than fetch_add in Experiment 4.
@enduml
